export anchor RomanInscriptionStyle:
    number: 145
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Roman inscription
    idea: The dashboard is a marble temple front, with the brand carved in a pediment, the four totals on fluted columns and each project cut into an inscribed tablet with dovetail handles.
    base: light
    palette:
        marble: #f4f2ec, the page, with faint grey veining from a noise texture
        vein: #dedad0, veins and the column dividing the chart weeks
        tablet: #ebe7dd, tablets, slabs, the architrave and fields
        cutStone: #2f2b25, carved lettering and body text
        slate: #57514a, secondary text, nav links and last week bars
        porphyry: #7a2626, the primary button, overdue, Behind and focus
        bronze: #73541a, progress fills, this week bars, roman numerals, the avatar medal and At risk
        laurel: #3d5a33, the wreath and On track
        groove: #c9c2b2, frames, mouldings and grooves, never text
    type:
        Inscriptional capitals in Optima, Optima Nova, Candara, Trajan
        Pro, Palatino Linotype, serif, always uppercase and tracked 0.14
        to 0.42em, carved with a white highlight below and a faint dark
        line above. Text uses Palatino Linotype, Book Antiqua, Palatino,
        Georgia, serif. The pediment brand is 30px tracked 0.42em, the
        greeting 56px, column figures 54px, tablet titles 17px, labels 12
        to 14px, body 16px at 1.55, subtitles italic.
    layout:
        Centred on one axis up to 1240px. A shallow triangular pediment
        spans the top with BRIGHTWORK carved in it. Under it an
        architrave band carries the caps nav split by interpuncts with a
        red underline on Home, then an inset search, the porphyry New
        project button, a square bell and a bronze medal avatar with the
        name. The greeting is centred, a laurel wreath over SALVE, MARA,
        the date in spaced caps and a tabula ansata plaque with 4 TASKS
        ARE OVERDUE in porphyry. A colonnade of four fluted columns, each
        with a capital with round volutes, a white plaque holding the
        figure and its roman numeral, the label below and a base with a
        cast shadow. Projects are six tablets in three columns, each with
        dovetail handles at both sides, a double inner frame, the category
        above the carved title, a carved groove progress bar with a bronze
        fill, three facts and the status under a rule. Below, two framed
        slabs, the chart with bars inset like carving and the weeks split
        by a stone column, and Acta diurna, the activity log with caps
        names and caps times. On phones the columns go two by two and the
        tablets stack.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between columns, 28 by 60px between tablets to leave room for handles, 48px between bands.
    density: Sparse and monumental.
    corners: Square stone. Tablets have dovetail handles on both sides and capitals have round volutes.
    borders: Mouldings as inner frames, a 1px groove line, an 8px gap and another groove. Double rules under the architrave.
    shadows: Inset shadows for carved text, grooves and fields, and a soft cast shadow under column bases.
    icons:
        Plain line icons for tools. Status uses Roman interpuncts, a round
        dot for On track, a triangle for At risk and a square for Behind,
        beside the spaced caps word.
    focus: A 2px porphyry outline offset 3px.
    tone: Inscriptional and brief, such as Salve, Mara and Acta diurna, with plain English for the facts.
